.TH LIKEOS-BOOTMENU.CONF 5 "November 2026" "LikeOS" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
likeos-bootmenu.conf \- the boot menu of the LikeOS installation medium
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B \eEFI\eLIKEOS\ebootmenu.conf
on the EFI system partition
.SH DESCRIPTION
The LikeOS boot loader
.RB ( BOOTX64.EFI )
shows a menu before it starts the kernel when the EFI system partition it
was loaded from has the file
.BR \eEFI\eLIKEOS\ebootmenu.conf .
The USB medium LikeOS is written to has one, with the entries
.B Run LikeOS Live from USB
and
.BR "Install LikeOS from USB" ;
a LikeOS installed on a disk has none, and starts straight away.
.PP
The menu is drawn on the firmware's graphics screen (as text where there is
none).
Up and Down choose an entry, Home and End the first and the last, a digit
the entry of that number (1 the first); Enter starts the chosen entry.
Until a key is pressed a countdown runs, and when it ends the default entry
starts.
.PP
The file is UTF-8 text, one setting per line.
Lines starting with
.B #
are comments; empty lines are ignored; blanks around a line are ignored.
.TP
.BI timeout= seconds
How long the menu waits before it starts the default entry.
.TP
.BI default= index
The entry chosen when the menu appears and started when the countdown
ends, counted from 0 in the order of the
.B entry
lines (default 0, the first).
.TP
.BI title= text
The heading of the menu.
.TP
.BI entry= title\fB|\fIwords
One menu entry, in the order of the file: the
.I title
the menu shows, a vertical bar, and the
.I words
the entry adds to the kernel command line (they may be empty).
The kernel and the system it starts see them in
.BR /proc/cmdline .
.SH KERNEL COMMAND LINE WORDS
.TP
.B likeos.mode=install
.BR init (8)
starts LikeOS Setup,
.BR likeos-installer (1),
on the console instead of the login prompt (it reads
.B /etc/inittab.install
instead of
.BR /etc/inittab ).
.TP
.B efi=noruntime
The kernel does not call the firmware's runtime services: no UEFI variables
in
.B /sys/firmware/efi/efivars
(for firmware that misbehaves; boot entries cannot be changed then).
.SH EXAMPLE
The file on the USB medium:
.PP
.RS
.nf
# The boot menu of the LikeOS USB medium
title=LikeOS
timeout=10
default=0
entry=Run LikeOS Live from USB|
entry=Install LikeOS from USB|likeos.mode=install
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR likeos-installer (1),
.BR likeos-install (1),
.BR likeos-efiboot (1)
